摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"DSH (DeepSeek Harness) plugin: per-session cost line + cost attribution report, priced by llm-pricing","id":"gh:1335786799","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-bill","slug":"Jannchie/dsh-bill","topics":["cost-attribution","cost-tracking","deepseek","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","llm","plugin","pricing","token-usage"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"DSH (DeepSeek Harness) plugin: per-session cost line + cost attribution report, priced by llm-pricin"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"SH (DeepSeek Harness) plugin: per-session cost line + cost attribution report, priced by llm-pricing"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-bill"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English | 中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Cost tracking for DSH (DeepSeek Harness). A line under each turn tells you what that turn cost; the "},{"id":"p4s2","text":"conversation's **Cost** tab tells you what that session's money went on, and the global **Cost** pan"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"el beside Plugins does the same for the whole account."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"Restart `dsh web` to pick it up."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"## Features"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"- **Cost attribution** — the bill split by kind of content: tool output, model output, system prompt"},{"id":"p9s2","text":", terminal commands (grouped by `git` / `pnpm` / `rg`), tool input, attachments, system reminders, u"},{"id":"p9s3","text":"ser input. The sunburst drills in.\n- **Per-turn cost** — one line under every finished turn: what it"},{"id":"p9s4","text":" cost, how many steps, the cache-hit rate. It reads the session log itself, so turns from before you"},{"id":"p9s5","text":" installed the plugin are covered too. A call a plugin makes on its own, outside any session (such a"},{"id":"p9s6","text":"s an auto-review before a tool call), belongs to no turn: it is in the account total and shows as a "},{"id":"p9s7","text":"separate *No session* row in the per-session split, so the turn lines can add up to less than the ac"},{"id":"p9s8","text":"count total.\n- **Always on screen** — this session's cost as a pill beside the shipped stats in the "},{"id":"p9s9","text":"composer dock, today's spend against the budget in the sidebar, and each session's cost in its sideb"},{"id":"p9s10","text":"ar hover card (DSH 0.1.7+). The dock's figure moves while a turn is still running, from the output t"},{"id":"p9s11","text":"hat has streamed so far, and becomes the billed figure the moment the provider reports it. Each of t"},{"id":"p9s12","text":"he five surfaces — and the report's icon in the sidebar panel row — can be turned off individually i"},{"id":"p9s13","text":"n settings.\n- **Report** — a **Cost** tab in each conversation (beside Chat and Trajectory) scoped t"},{"id":"p9s14","text":"o that session, and an account-wide **Cost** panel opened from the sidebar icon beside Plugins (DSH "},{"id":"p9s15","text":"0.1.7+): total, tokens, cache hit, peak share; account-wide also monthly forecast, account balance, "},{"id":"p9s16","text":"budget and a per-session split; broken down by model and by purpose (including loop overhead such as"},{"id":"p9s17","text":" context compaction); spend over time stacked by model, with each bar's split on hover; a weekday × "},{"id":"p9s18","text":"hour heatmap. The window is either rolling (the last 24 hours, 7, 30, 90 or 365 days) or a calendar "},{"id":"p9s19","text":"day (today, yesterday) on the host's clock, plus all time; bars are hours for a day or less, then da"},{"id":"p9s20","text":"ys, weeks or months as the window grows.\n- **Budget** — a daily / monthly / all-time limit that turn"},{"id":"p9s21","text":"s amber past 80% and red when you go over.\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## How it differs from similar plugins"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"Three substantive differences:"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"**No hand-maintained price table.** Every other plugin ships a built-in table of 2–4 DeepSeek models"},{"id":"p12s2","text":", which means no prices at all once you switch provider — and which is why they all need a \"edit the"},{"id":"p12s3","text":" price table by hand\" entry point. dsh-bill pulls models.dev and OpenRouter through `llm-pricing`, c"},{"id":"p12s4","text":"overing 8000+ entries, so a new model is priced the day it ships."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"**Price is a timeline, not a number.** The others compute a cost and store it (or recompute at today"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"'s price), so history goes wrong the moment a vendor changes its rates or a call crosses a peak/off-"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"peak boundary. dsh-bill prices each call at that call's own instant, and never recomputes history."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"**It answers \"on what\".** The others answer only \"how much\" — they consume the provider's aggregate "},{"id":"p14s2","text":"token counts and never look at the request content. dsh-bill splits the request into classified segm"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"ents at capture time and apportions cost by position in the cache prefix."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"They do some things better: `usage-stats` reads balances and subscription quotas from 11 providers ("},{"id":"p15s2","text":"dsh-bill only does DeepSeek), `cost-meter` can read OpenCode Go's subscription quota, and both surfa"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"ce more always-on entry points than dsh-bill does."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"Point-by-point comparison (read from source, sampled 2026-08-16)"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"The sample is the cost-related plugins under the GitHub `dsh-plugin` topic with ★ ≥ 40, plus the fou"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"r published to npm. Lower-starred plugins such as `deepseek-harness-wallet` were not checked individ"},{"id":"p17s3","text":"ished to npm. Lower-starred plugins such as `deepseek-harness-wallet` were not checked individually."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"| | dsh-bill | cost-meter | usage-stats | dsh-cost | cost-log | dsh-usage | usage-billing |"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"| stars / version | — | ★42 / 1.3.1 | ★40 / 0.2.0 | ★3 / 0.2.1 | ★2 / 1.0.0 | ★2 / 0.1.1 | 0.2.2 |\n|"},{"id":"p19s2","text":" price source | online catalogue | built-in table + hand-scraped docs | none | built-in table | buil"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"t-in table | user-entered | built-in table |\n| models covered | 8000+ entries | 4 DeepSeek | — | 4 D"},{"id":"p19s4","text":"eepSeek | 2 DeepSeek | one at a time, by hand | DeepSeek |\n| unlisted model | flagged, excluded from"},{"id":"p19s5","text":" totals | billed at flash rate | flagged unknown | billed as v4-pro | flagged `≈` | flagged `--` | c"},{"id":"p19s6","text":"ounted as 0 |\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"## Pricing"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"- two catalogues, models.dev and OpenRouter, cached for 24h and written to disk, falling back to a b"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"uilt-in historical snapshot on failure;\n- DeepSeek's own direct rates override the catalogue, and th"},{"id":"p21s3","text":"e peak / off-peak rate is chosen from the call's timestamp;\n- a prompt-cache write is priced at the "},{"id":"p21s4","text":"lifetime the provider reports it bought: when the usage report carries `cacheWrite1hTokens` (the one"},{"id":"p21s5","text":"-hour share of `cacheWriteTokens`, which Anthropic returns for a route that asks for the long cache)"},{"id":"p21s6","text":", that share is billed as a one-hour write and the rest as a five-minute write; without it every wri"},{"id":"p21s7","text":"te is a five-minute write;\n- model names are normalised, and anything that still fails to match is f"},{"id":"p21s8","text":"lagged `?` and excluded from totals — nothing is estimated;\n- `priceOverrides` can override or add a"},{"id":"p21s9","text":"ny price (rarely needed)."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"## Attribution method"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"Every request pays for the full context again, so one tool output read into the conversation keeps b"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"eing billed on every subsequent request until it slides out of the window. Attribution is computed p"},{"id":"p23s3","text":"er request and summed."},{"id":"p24s1","text":"Two things matter:"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"## Configuration"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"## Data and privacy"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"- each call's provider / model / token usage and attributed amounts are written to `$DSH_HOME/dsh-bi"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"ll/records.jsonl` (a 20 000-entry ring buffer; older entries are folded into a rollup);\n- the API ke"},{"id":"p29s3","text":"y used for the account balance is read and used host-side and never reaches the browser;\n- nothing i"},{"id":"p29s4","text":"s sent anywhere except the price catalogues, the exchange-rate endpoint, and the balance query; no c"},{"id":"p29s5","text":"onversation content is stored."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}

